Z||000005||2xsess||12-17-2000||12:28 PM||||Boy there's just so many. <P>1958 Willys CJ5, traded it for a POS Transam because the Jeep only had a top speed of 45mph.<P>My first Fiero, 1984 base coupe, I bought tech rims for it and added a GT spoiler. The car was near mint condition until some older man on too many prescriptions ran over the line on a blind corner and totalled it.<P>1988 FieroGT t-top, I bought it wrecked from Kickhill and had it almost complete minus paint on the winshield pillar. Traded it in when I met my wife and needed backseat for her kids.<P>1990 Celica GTS, yea it was only a 2.2 4cylinder but it was pretty quick and it had a factory 10 speaker stereo system with an amp under the seat and am/fm cassette/cd.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||12-17-2000||12:49 PM||||'55, two 56's and a '57 Chevy, '55 and '57 T-Bird, '65 GTO............too many to think of -- if only I had known then what I know now............||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||12-17-2000||12:58 PM||||I miss my 78 Malibu coupe. Sure, its 305 V8 was a POS and it couldn't hold an alignment, but if I only had it now... can you say 350?<P>Now, if my dad got on this topic, whoo-wee!  Lets see... Model A roadster pickup, 1953 Olds Super 88, 55 Caddy sedan deville, 67 Nova SS, 1971 Formula 400, 1975 DeTamaso Pantera, 1965 Corvair wagon, 1982 VW Scirocco GTi (European version)...<BR>sigh.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DrRodey||12-17-2000||01:02 PM||||Only two... 94 Grand Prix GTP.. God i loved that car.. all it needed was a manual transmission and it would have been perfect. Totaled it on my way to a snowboarding weekend near Duluth. Damn Black Ice.<P>And i too miss my 92 Geo Storm GSi.  They are cute little cars. not too much power but still fun to drive.<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">     <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||2M4 Dale||12-17-2000||01:11 PM||||I've had quite a few that I wish I had back but the worst two are :<P>67 GTO Convertible that was my first car...I traded it off for a 64 Gran Prix and $300.<BR>I never drove the GP and I sold it for $500 and in retrospect what a mistake !<P>The second one, and probably the biggest mistake, was tradeing my 1969 GTO Judge for a Winnabago......We had some fun in the Winny but it's gone and probably worth nothing and the Judge is a show winner and probably worth $20,000 at least.||||reg||9
Z||000010||KnightRyder31||12-17-2000||01:55 PM||||My hopped up Bonneville SSEI...loved that car.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick's Dad||12-17-2000||02:05 PM||||My second car, a 1973 Camaro LT. 4BBL SBC.... Got decked by a motorcycle  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  It hit the car in the driver's front wheel and bent the frame (I was too young to realize that this might be fixable). The thing I remember best from the accident is the teardrop tank from the cycle flying into a yard across the four lane road....<P>Thankfully, the driver and passenger of the motorcycle jumped off before it hit my car. I got out and said, "Are you alright?" and he said, "I was going to ask you the same thing!" He had been cut off by a small car and bolted left to avoid her, but lost control and the bike crossed the road.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Sage||12-17-2000||02:16 PM||||1957 Chevy Belair 2dr hrdtp<BR>283 punched to 288<BR>custom 4bolt main block <BR>12 1/2 to 1 forged aluminum pistons<BR>balanced-blue printed<BR>phase III z28 cam<BR>fender well exit headers<BR>1150cfm holley on aluminum hi rise<BR>custom zoom clutch<BR>muncie 4 spd<BR>5:13 gears<BR>12.50 @128mph in the quarter mi.<BR>Those were the days!<P>68 Triumph TR250(6cyl) fun car!<P>72 MGB GT  Even had a "back seat".<P>Miss em' all.<P>Have a good one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Slammed Fiero||12-17-2000||02:18 PM||||We had a 66 corvair 4 door , 4spd with a caorsa 180hp Turbo , car was lowered , blue and silver , had caddy disk brakes .. Free flow exhaust and a sidedraft webber carb... <BR>it was driven everyday from 80 to 91 , rust took it's toll after we stored the litle monster and we parted it out...<P>Still have the motor , tranny and brakes in the garage..<P>alas.. memories..<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||12-17-2000||02:21 PM||||stimpy wrote<P>"Now, if my dad got on this topic, whoo-wee! Lets see, 1965 Corvair wagon, 1982 VW Scirocco GTi (European version)...<BR>sigh."<P><BR>The only built the corvair wagon in 61 and 62. It was called a "Lakewood" in 61 and a "Monza" wagon in 62.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
