Z||000021||fierosound||12-17-2000||06:43 PM||||I must be a sucker for discontinued GM models!  One of the fastest I had was 1979 Chev Monza Spyder V8-4speed.  I swapped the crappy 268ci small block with a 365hp 350 V8, just dropped right in!  With poly bushings in the suspension etc., it handled like it was on rails, and beat almost anything trying me at the light.  But, when the body started to rust out...  time to get something newer.  <P>My 1987 Fiero GT 5-speed replaced it.  With it's new 3.4L I just dropped in, I now have that same feeling of invincible power in a car that handles considerably better. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/tonys87.htm</A> <P>I've had it 11 years now.  With the new engine, it should be good for another 15...<P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||zeusrekning||12-17-2000||07:48 PM||||71 lemans. Engine was in mint condition interior was mint, paint was a little faded but ok.<BR>Girl pulled out in front of me on a gravel road in a mitcubitchy eclipse. I pretty much put the drives side wheel and strut on the pass side.<BR>Car was nastiest shade of green. But i put  a completely custom interior in it. ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Cheever2||12-17-2000||09:22 PM||||<B>'68 VW Baja Bug</B> I built from ground up.  Tried to make it a daily driver and compromised too much offroad vs. street.  Next time it will be just for street.  Sold it to the guy that built the engine.<P><B>'66 Mustang 289</B>.  Everything started falling apart all at once, so got a good tradein on a new Subaru just after getting married.<P><B>'77 Scout SSII</B>.  I had a 304 V8, sold it to my 4-wheeling buddy, he blew that engine and put in a 345 with Hooker headers and Holley double-pumper.  He got trophies in amatuer tractor pulls until he blew that motor also.  But I always wish I'd kept it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||rockcrawl||12-17-2000||09:23 PM||||2xsess, I know what you mean about the 58 Willys with a 45mph top speed, I still have one. The 305 chevy doesn't make it go any faster when it has 5.38:1 gears!<P>I miss my '69 327 Camaro, and of course the Countach!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
