Z||000026||My7Fieros||12-17-2000||11:24 PM||||My 1978 Trans Am. My dad bought it new in 78 and gave it to me in 89 during my junior year in high school...I traded her in in 95 for a 95 Camaro  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ..temp brain fart I guess. WHAT A DUMB MOVE! She was silver w/ red interior and looked and ran BEAUTIFULLY! Come to find out that the mechanic at the Chevrolet dealership bought it right then and there..hopefully he is taking (or took) good care of her!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Also cant forget my 84 Fiero I had during my sophmore year in highschool in 88....oh well, actually sold that to do some things to my Trans Am that I was getting ready to get!||||reg||1
Z||000027||terryk||12-18-2000||12:10 AM||||67 Cyclone GT. 390 4 spd. Dang!<P>Looking for an Avanti.||||reg||1
Z||000028||Songman||12-18-2000||01:32 AM||||My most missed car was my red 1985 911 Targa. This was the car that I had dreamed about for a long time. Finally got it and I was in heaven! Went home to visit my family in GA one Christmas and a guy who was turning left tried to beat traffic as the light changed. What he didn't plan on was that I was approaching the light at about 40 mph. Our front corners hit and spun me and tore the whole side of my car out, including pushing the rear half shaft into the tranny. Of course, he informed me that I was lucky he was in his wife's Granada instead of his 4x4 truck because I would have gone under it. And as if that wasn't enough reason to kill him.... when he found out that I was a country music singer, he started asking me to get people's autographs for him! I hope he is still holding his breath!<P>Anyway.. I miss that car!||||reg||9
Z||000029||wkayl||12-18-2000||01:53 AM||||My first car was a 1953 Ford Mainline 4-door that you had to check the gas and fill with oil. But it did start pretty good if you had a hill to roll down. I graduated up to a 1955 Ford my Jr. year in high school. I went to town to buy a battery for it and ended up with a 1961 Studebaker Lark XIII for the same price as a battery. After graduating high school I bought another 61 Studebaker Lark XIII Cruiser and still have it today (it even passed Colorado emissions). In the mid 70's I had many of the cars people dream about today. They included (2) 67 GTOs, (2) 67 Mustangs, (1) 71 Challenger R/T, (1) 71 Nova SS, (1) 67 Firebird, and the one that makes me sick that I sold it for $880.00, a 70 AAR Cuda. I ended the 70's keeping a 1967 Buick Skylark conv that I also still have today. <P>You can read my entire bio on FieroDave's web site at:<BR> <A HREF="http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/wayne.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/wayne.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||terryk||12-18-2000||02:00 AM||||In 70, I did get to drive an LS5 Nova SS. A kids dad special ordered it. One scary car....||||reg||1
Z||000031||onfire||12-18-2000||04:32 AM||||1978 Trans-Am my first car.<BR>6.6l v8 automatic wish it was a four speed.<P>1985 Fiero GT 2.8l v6 four speed glad it wasn't an automatic.<P>My uncle used to have some awesome cars 1975 Trans-Am, 69 Dodge Super Bee with a 440 six-pack, wow both of those cars were insanely fast.<P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000032||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||04:18 PM||||'79 Corvette, bought it for $800 when i was 14... worked on it for little over 2 years.. had it with my new liscense for 3 full weeks then the day it came home from the Paint shop i got nailed for speeding... i was PROMPTLY forced to sell it.. I loved that car.. got a 402 from a guy out of Hemmings for $600 got a rebuilt Holley 900-3 barrel for $200 and it would SCREAM!! Muncie 4 speed... Vermillion on Oyster hides... only had MAYBE $5k in it.. 6 months later i got my liscense back from the state and bought a 95 4x4 Ranger Splash (orange) what a mistake that was! 18k on the clock and slept in the shop for 80% of my owning it... Never gunna buy another one of those... (i know it's not ALL their fault.. but still) <P><BR>Phil... NICE RIDE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  my dad had a series 1 with a 3.8 and a 4.2!!  traded them for a 7? (tall grill) XJ12L.. still not sure who got the better trade...  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000033||GeeDee86GT||12-18-2000||06:13 PM||||83 Skoda... nah!<BR>'72 Fiat 124 spider.  1600 cc DOHC 5 spd. Put 75,000 miles on it in Cape Breton in a year and a half.  Redline at 6500 RPM and I think I hit it every shift.  Bags 'o fun!<BR>For speed '67 Mustang convertible 390 4 speed. Went through Montreal at over 100 MPH one night and some nut in a Ferrari 308 passed me on the right verge like I was standing still.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/garby_d/siggy.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000034||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||12-19-2000||03:29 AM||||I had a 1989 Dodge Colt GT turbo, bought it brand new.<P>Before you roll your eyes and say "one of those SOHC econo-boxes" consider that you are thinking of the previous generation car.<P>The 1989 had a 16 valve turbo motor that could do 0 to 60 in a little over 7 seconds. It had no speed governor so you could get into the 130s.  And, it usually got about 30 mpg if you stayed under 90 mph.  <P>But then, at 47k miles the timing belt broke and the motor was never the same again.  I traded it in with 90K miles and it was burning oil and had low compression in one cylinder.  The angry hair dryer was no more.<P>I will never forget that little car.  But, I would never buy another one.  Kind of like the Maserati Biturbo my dad used to have.  I wonder if he knows how many times I took it out on joy rides . . . The Maserati was one hell of a sleeper.<P>Then there was the 1993 Cavalier Z24 I owned for a few years.  It wasn't much of a performance car, but the red paint and throaty exhaust were extremely cool.  <P>Given the choice, I would still rather take one more insane ride in the 1989 Colt Turbo.  It was a car like no other.  I was lucky to keep my liscence!||||reg||1
Z||000035||Xtreme Fiero's||12-19-2000||04:29 AM||||<BR>1989 Camaro IROC Z-28, LT1, Auto T-Tops Traded it for a '94 Z31 300ZX TT 2+2 (that turned out to have un repairable frame damage)<P>'94 300 ZX TT 2+2 DOH!!!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000036||ChadMan||12-19-2000||09:06 AM||||I miss this car every single day of my life.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000216.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000216.html</A> <P>And I still don't own a home.||||reg||9
Z||000037||Predator||12-19-2000||09:18 AM||||My first car was a 1970 Ford Torino GT. It had a 429 Police Intercepter engine and trans from a LTD State Trouper car. Needless to say I had a whole lot more respect for the State Patrol after owning that car. I have never had a car since that ran like that thing did. ||||reg||1
