Z||000039||sparks||12-19-2000||11:02 AM||||1968 Firebird, 350 Muncie 4 speed, Hurst shifter.  Dang I miss that car.<P>Sold it for a 69 Commando with a 225 V6, miss that one too.<P>Still have the 62 CJ-5, with the aforementioned top speed of 45 mph!  NOT parting with that one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>And of course my first and only Fiero that I've grown to like so much over the past two months, 85 SC.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||10
Z||000040||PearlBlueSoul||12-19-2000||03:05 PM||||AAah my 86 MR2...first car, and I gave that car so much hell.  geez, man I drove it hard. <P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/mr2drs/images/mr2-front%20r%20dist.jpg">   <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">         <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.<P>[This message has been edited by PearlBlueSoul (edited 12-19-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by PearlBlueSoul (edited 12-19-2000).]||||reg||1
